    "reason": "The English lemma 'dress' (noun) most commonly refers to a one-piece garment worn by women. The Japanese expression '衣紋' (えもん) refers to the drapery or folds of clothing, especially a kimono, or the style of wearing clothes. It does not refer to the garment itself. The JMdict glosses provided in the prompt ('dress', 'clothes') appear to be an inaccurate simplification of the actual JMdict entry for '衣紋', which lists 'drapery (of clothes)', 'folds (of a kimono)', and 'style of wearing clothes'. Therefore, it is semantically incorrect for the concept of 'dress' as a garment.",
